## Why This Is Asked
Tests threat modeling and practical controls for log integrity across cloud boundaries, a common fintech risk.

## Key Concepts
- Log integrity, STRIDE/PASTA, SBOM, log signing, KMS, append-only storage, WORM, cross-cloud replication, SIEM/SOAR, tabletop exercises

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo code for signing log entries
function signLogEntry(entry, key) {
  const signature = crypto.sign("SHA256", Buffer.from(JSON.stringify(entry)), key);
  return { entry, signature };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you verify integrity of logs during audits across clouds?
- How would you coordinate key rotation and revocation in a distributed SIEM?

## Why This Is Asked
Addresses detection/containment of DNS exfiltration in multi-cloud, a gap in the existing questions.

## Key Concepts
- DNS exfiltration patterns (long queries, high entropy)
- Cross‑cloud log sources (AWS Route 53 Resolver logs, IBM DNS, Cloudflare Gateway logs)
- SIEM correlation (Splunk/QRadar)
- Containment actions (Cloudflare Gateway blocking, firewall rules) and IR coordination

## Code Example
```javascript
function dnsExfiltrationDetected(log) {
  const longQuery = log.query.length > 60;
  const highEntropy = /[A-Za-z0-9+/]{60,}/.test(log.query);
  const unusualTLD = /\.(xyz|top|icu|cc)$/i.test(log.domain);
  return longQuery && highEntropy && unusualTLD;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you tune FP/FN rates across clouds?
- How would you test the IR playbook without impacting business?
